    {
      "id": 70,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        -780
      ],
      "size": [
        1600,
        680
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 47,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# UltraTex · 10 INPUT IMAGES -> 3D BAKE (NO AI ALBEDO GENERATION)\n\nThis is a modified version of the supplied 10-view + PBR workflow.\n\n**Six canonical photos:** front, left, back, right, top, bottom.\n\n**Four additional photos:** yaw 45°, 135°, 225°, 315°.\n\nAssign ALL TEN files in the LoadImage nodes, and set the mesh path. Then Run.\n\nThe Albedo AI Samplers are REMOVED: the ten provided RGB photos are projected directly onto the mesh UVs.\n\n**Important:** the provided images must already have camera alignment with the corresponding views of the provided 3D mesh: same camera angles, FOV/perspective and object framing. The workflow does NOT solve camera registration automatically. Arbitrary real-world photos will often misproject. The image is center-cropped to 1024² but not geometrically calibrated.\n\nThe bottom-right PBR branch still uses AI to estimate Metallic/Roughness from the front reference. Remove the MR-to-Bake connection to skip AI entirely (then export only Albedo).\n\nSecond rig is 45° rotated. The repeated top/bottom images are placeholders only: Bake sets `views_2_use=no top/bottom` so only its first four rotated views are used.\n"
      ],
      "title": "README / manual 10-view projection",
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    },
    {
      "id": 71,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2410,
        -780
      ],
      "size": [
        1200,
        680
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 48,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Bake input `albedo_views` receives 6 native views through ImageBatch.\nBake input `albedo_views_2` receives 4 user-supplied rotated side views + 2 ignored duplicates.\n2 custom nodes for mesh/rig/bake are unchanged; the model generation samplers for ALBEDO were removed.\n\nOutput: ComfyUI/output/UltraTex/Manual10*.glb and PNG Albedo, plus ORM if the optional MR sampler runs.\n\nThis JSON was statically checked for consistent ComfyUI graph links, but actual run needs the UltraTex custom nodes and model files installed.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Output & validation",
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    }
